        "assignees": [],
        "author_association": "MEMBER",
        "body": "Saving a workout set the Activity view to `list` while the app's own landing view had moved to `lanes` (Overview), so finishing a log dropped onto a different page than opening the app did. Both paths now read a single `DEFAULT_ACTIVITY_VIEW` constant.\n\nNot a regression from the earlier landing-page work: that change moved the mount default and never touched the post-save path, which had been `list` since #19.\n\nScope: create path only. Edits (`onWorkoutChanged`/`onCardioChanged`) refresh in place, and the soreness editor still returns to its launch point.\n\n## Verification\n\n`npm run lint`, `npm test` (7/7), and `npm run build` all pass in `frontend/`. The save path itself was not exercised end-to-end — the dev backend talks to the live Cosmos DB, so that would mean writing a real workout.",
